{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>We are journeying.</b> Rashi explained that Moses joined himself with them — the decree had not yet been issued, and he thought he would enter, as stated in the portion of Exodus where Rashi explained 'send, I pray you, by the hand of him whom You will send' — his end is not to bring them into the land. And according to the plain sense, Moses joined himself with them, saying: now Israel will say, if he who performed signs and brought us out of Egypt and did for us wonders and mighty acts does not enter, how shall we enter? Another interpretation: on account of Jethro, so that he not say: if Moses does not enter, how shall I enter?" "<b>And we will do you good.</b> From the spoil; but to give him a portion in the land, they had no authority."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The abbreviation חז״ק has been resolved as 'as stated' (חזר וכתב / חז״י קאמר), though the exact expansion is uncertain; the reference is to Rashi's comment on Exodus."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:18.024785550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}